{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://aureline.dev/schemas/content/freeze-the-m5-content-design-controlled-vocabulary-content-ops-and-commercial-boundary-wording-matrix.schema.json",
  "title": "Aureline M5 content-design, controlled-vocabulary, content-ops metadata, and commercial-boundary wording matrix",
  "description": "Export-safe packet freezing the canonical M5 product-wording object model. The packet names every governed wording or content object — the safety-critical UI string, the controlled glossary term, the action-label pattern, the error/recovery block, the AI copy guardrail, the count/scope phrase set, the content-ops metadata artifact, and the commercial-boundary wording review — and binds each to its qualification class, required fields, the controlled state vocabularies it carries, the concrete vocabulary tokens it admits, evidence requirements, the proof packet that keeps it current, downgrade triggers, rollback posture, source contracts, and consumer-surface parity. A self-describing vocabulary set freezes the controlled vocabulary for lifecycle, trust, policy, compatibility, freshness, client scope, hosting boundary, and managed/local/self-hosted/open edition labels. Raw message bodies, raw provider payloads, credentials, secret material, and untranslated free-text prose never cross this boundary.",
